  "Number": 8,
  "Question": "What is the probability that a randomly drawn positive factor of \\(60\\) is less than \\(7?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{10}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{6}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{4}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{3}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "List factors in pairs whose product is \\(60\\):\n\\[\n(1,60),\\ (2,30),\\ (3,20),\\ (4,15),\\ (5,12),\\ (6,10).\n\\]\nThis list is complete because every factor pair must have a member less than \\(8\\), since \\(8^2>60\\). We have checked every positive integer through \\(7\\), and \\(7\\) does not divide \\(60\\).\n\nThese pairs contain \\(12\\) distinct positive factors. Exactly \\(1,2,3,4,5,6\\) are less than \\(7\\). Since each factor is equally likely to be drawn, the probability is\n\\[\n\\frac{6}{12}=\\boxed{\\frac12}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice E.",
